<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ssangseong Prefecture</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1258–1356</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Ssangseong Commandery</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ssangseong Prefecture was an administrative district set up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1258 in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, around modern Kumya and Yonghung, after local Korean officials defected to them. It remained under Yuan control for almost a century. In 1356 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gongmin-of-goryeo">King Gongmin</a> of Goryeo recovered it by force, helped by the local commander Yi Ja-chun, father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taejo-of-joseon">Yi Seong-gye</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ssangseong-prefecture.jpg" alt="Ssangseong Prefecture" width="320" height="523" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 고려 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%9B%90_%EA%B0%84%EC%84%AD%EA%B8%B0_%EC%8B%9C%EA%B8%B0%EC%9D%98_%EA%B3%A0%EB%A0%A4.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
